CommitDate: Sun Sep 20 19:26:08 2026 -0500

    fix: 429 backpressure is retried, and init no longer crashes on an error body. Addresses AUG-006.
    
    The tier-1 judge failed AUG-006 for a real reason the worker's own run could not
    see: under the guard, gate.sh runs pytest AND smoke.sh, and the combined burst
    trips DuckBrain's token-bucket limiter (600 req/min, live-measured). The 429
    propagated straight through the transport, so cmd_init read an ERROR body as a
    namespace list, crashed with `'str' object has no attribute 'get'`, and left the
    namespace it had just created behind.
    
    A 429 is BACKPRESSURE, not a failure. _req now retries it inline (up to 4 times,
    honouring the server's own retryAfter / Retry-After, bounded linear backoff),
    before any caller sees a status. cmd_init additionally fails loudly on a non-200
    list instead of parsing the error dict — an init that reports success while
    declaring nothing is worse than one that stops.
    
    Proven deterministically, because the original failure is load-dependent and did
    not reproduce in a quiet run: with the bucket saturated by a background hammer,
    the HOLED transport (retry branch forced off) returns 429 to the caller while the
    fixed one returns 200 — measured, same saturation, same second. The holed branch
    is also the RED control for the regression the previous failure exhibited.
    
    Also recorded while investigating: `_token()` sends x-api-key, which is correct
    (Bearer on this endpoint returns 401 — re-measured here), and the shared
    /api/namespaces registry accumulates rows for namespaces whose directory is gone
    (19 stale test entries were cleared by hand; teardown deletes both paths when it
    runs, which is why the suite reports api+disk clean on a passing run).
